ready: 1
kind: rule
id: identity.rule.drift
display_id: RULE-IDENTITY-DRIFT
module: identity
title: How far recent behavior has moved from stated identity
summary: >-
  Compares what the agent recently did and concluded with its values and self-narrative, and reports drift
  with the memories that show it.
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/identity/drift.rs::detect
inputs:
- name: recent memories
  source: Episodes, beliefs, and goal changes from the drift window
  source_kind: stored
- name: stated identity
  source: Active values and the active self-narrative
  source_kind: stored
constants:
- identity.const.drift-window
- identity.const.drift-alert
calculations:
- name: alignment of a recent memory
  expr: >-
    max cosine between the memory and any value or narrative theme; contradicting links count as zero
    alignment
- name: drift
  expr: >-
    1 − salience-weighted mean alignment of recent memories, plus 0.1 for each value whose supporting
    beliefs were superseded in the window, capped at 1
when: Drift is at or above the alert score
then: The report marks drift as significant and lists the most divergent memories as examples
otherwise: The report shows the drift score with examples, marked as within normal change
default: No drift (0) when the window holds no memories
rationale: >-
  Drift is reported, never corrected automatically. Growth looks like drift from the outside, and only
  the agent or owner can tell a change of character from a lapse.
